  "claims": {
    "classification": "Proved obstruction to coarse-data constant exclusion using genuine smooth NS finite segments; bounded two-candidate strategy review, not an NS regularity theorem",
    "formula_tags": {
      "BH": 18,
      "total": 18
    },
    "proved_in_stated_scope": [
      "There exist expanding periodic, unit-viscosity unforced smooth NS segments with zero mean, terminal unit peak, past sup <=1+o(1), cell energy O(period scale), normalized total dissipation tending to zero, and histories tending to infinity, converging locally uniformly through the terminal time to a unit constant vector.",
      "The construction uses a compact curl seed, unnormalized inhomogeneous H^m estimates uniform on large tori and for positive viscosity 1/n, a short original time window n^-1/2, and two exact NS rescalings. Standard local existence/continuation interfaces are invoked explicitly, not claimed fully re-proved.",
      "Energy and spacetime dissipation both multiply by q in final peak rescaling. Small normalized dissipation uses the uniform pointwise-in-time gradient bound, not the scalar energy identity alone.",
      "This refutes automatic exclusion of nonzero constant ancient limits from the listed coarse budgets even when each segment solves true NS. It does not reproduce a fixed initial datum, a genuine first blow-up, or an exact running record."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "For fixed initial data on period scale 1, complete peak history retains b_k/ell_k^2 -> T_*>0 and remote initial sup ->0. This construction instead has b_n/ell_n^2=n^-11/2 ->0 and initial sup ->1.",
